"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"required_mechanisms_exposed\":{\"deepinfer/environ.py\":{\"exposed\":0,\"registered\":3},\"deepinfer/logger.py\":{\"exposed\":0,\"registered\":3},\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\":{\"exposed\":0,\"registered\":4}}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'll set up the plan, then read all three required files and run the baseline check.\n\n```python\nupdate_plan([\n    {\"title\": \"Read required source files\", \"status\": \"doing\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement environ.py config\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement logger.py formatter budget\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement stats_logger.py extra flag\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run final pytest and produce patch/logs\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n])\nr1 = read_file(\"deepinfer/environ.py\")\nr2 = read_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\")\nr3 = read_file(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\")\nprint(len(r1['content']), r1['file_hash'])\nprint(len(r2['content']), r2['file_hash'])\nprint(len(r3['content']), r3['file_hash'])\nprint(r1['content'])\n```"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n8304 fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\n5534 5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\n19925 9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\n[versioned evidence retained separately]\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\":\"update_plan\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{}},{\"tool\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\"file_hash