ch.diff) exist? The previous action likely generated them. The progress says final_answer next. Let me do a quick check of files and then update plan and final answer.\n\nActually the instructions say when current action runs a required test and succeeds, update plan and call final_answer in same action. Tests already passed. Let me just quick-verify the patch.diff and run.log exist, then update plan and final_answer.\n\nBut careful: only one action left? \"requests_left\": 0. So I need to finalize now. I'll check artifacts quickly and final answer in same block — but final_answer must only be called after verification. Let me combine: check files exist, update plan, then final_answer... but final_answer inside conditional code is risky if verification fails. However I can compute and only call final_answer if checks pass; else print diagnostics.\n\nLet me do: read task_status? Not needed. Just check artifacts presence via run_command listing, update plan, and call final_answer.\n\nHmm, but if artifacts missing, I'd fail. Let's check with run_command ls and compute. I'll write code that checks, and only final_answer if artifacts present; otherwise print. Given limited requests, still.\n\nActually the progress phase says \"finish_plan\" meaning everything else complete including artifacts presumably. I'll just verify quickly and finalize."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 5845, "completion_tokens": 666, "total_tokens": 6511, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4096}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 311}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4096, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 1749}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
